The adaptation replaces synchronous requests with asynchronous HTTP, imports
Mesh profiles only during configuration, selects each node's bound network and
application keys, validates profiles, and does not retain login credentials or
session tokens. Cloud actuator calls and predictive algorithms are not included.
Core entity names and filter/heater dependencies follow the upstream integration.

Bluetooth Mesh transport is independently implemented from the protocol.
Published cryptographic test vectors were checked against Nordic Semiconductor's
Android nRF Mesh Library, reference commit:
